            <ArticleTitle>Acalculous cholecystitis in a patient with visceral leishmaniasis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>621-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute acalculous cholecystitis (ACC) is unusual. We present a case of cholecystitis associated with visceral leishmaniasis (VL) in a man in Venezuela who presented high fever, anorexia and abdominal pain. Histopathological study of the gallbladder showed Leishmania spp. ACC in VL must be kept in mind in tropical countries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
